<PageTitle>C13 · Architecture and workflow</PageTitle>
<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">ARCHITECTURE &amp; WORKFLOW</p><h1>From scenario to evidence</h1><p class="lead">Blazor Server keeps experiment execution, credentials, SDK calls, and the run journal on the .NET host.</p></div></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Application workflow</h2><p><a href="/architecture.svg" target="_blank">Open diagram</a> · <a href="/architecture.svg" download>Download SVG</a></p><img class="architecture" src="/architecture.svg" alt="Blazor browser connects to C# services. Local runs execute LessonEngine and append a journal; optional live commentary creates and streams an Anthropic Managed Agents session." style="width:100%;background:white;border-radius:12px" /></section>
<section class="card"><h2>1 · Prepare configuration</h2><p>The local path needs no remote resources. Optional setup creates the environment before the agent and saves each ID immediately. Existing IDs from configuration or the saved resource file are reused.</p>
<h2>2 · Collect and validate inputs</h2><p>Home.razor binds the scenario and three editable text fields. The same engine is available through POST /api/run and /api/live. The API enforces JSON, a 64 KB body limit, and same-origin requests; individual strings are limited to 20,000 UTF-16 characters.</p>
<h2>3 · Execute the experiment</h2><p>LessonEngine starts from three fixed parent events, rejects unknown boundaries, transfers events through the selected boundary, and computes SHA-256 hashes of UTF-8 text. It prepares a restoration plan and preserves the parent.</p>
<h2>4 · Record local evidence</h2><p>LabService permits one experiment at a time across browser circuits and API requests. Local results receive a run ID and append to .lab-data/runs.jsonl. Live commentary is displayed separately.</p>
<h2>5 · Request optional commentary</h2><p>ManagedAgentsService uses AnthropicClient.Beta.Sessions.Create with a text-only agent override, empty tools/MCP/skills, a $10 session budget ceiling and the experiment as an initial event. StreamStreaming observes messages, usage, and terminal status with a 60-second deadline and no retries. On failure it attempts an interrupt and reports that stopping is unconfirmed.</p>
<h2>6 · Execute live session scenarios</h2><p><a href="/live-sessions">Live sessions</a> calls SessionScenarioService and the AnthropicSessionGateway. Inventory reads one page with a cursor. Event reads follow ascending canonical history across pages. Branch preview binds reviewed context to a selected-history hash. Creating a branch rechecks that prefix, pins the parent agent version, and queues only accepted context into a new text-only session with lineage metadata.</p>
<p>Snapshots store canonical provider history bytes locally; mirrors append unseen event IDs after a durable write. Both reject conflicting event content. Live run records retain known created session IDs before observation begins. Missing boundaries create no child; incomplete reads cannot establish boundary absence. Failures attempt to interrupt only a newly created session and preserve remote stop uncertainty.</p>
<h2>7 · Verify the distinction</h2><p>Local experiments prepare plans. Commentary explains those plans. Live session scenarios perform provider operations and show their IDs and observed status. History snapshots and reviewed-context branches do not clone containers or restore remote files.</p></section>
